    "['isis network [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 point-to-point', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco \"isis network point-to-point\" command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 point-to-point\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 point-to-point\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper requires this to be set per interface under the IS-IS protocol configuration, whereas Cisco sets it directly in interface configuration mode. The translation assumes the Juniper interface names match the Cisco ones (ge-1/0/0 for GigabitEthernet1/0/0, etc.).', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 point-to-point'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 point-to-point', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco \"isis network point-to-point\" command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 point-to-point\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 point-to-point\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper requires this to be set per interface under the IS-IS protocol configuration, whereas Cisco sets it directly in interface configuration mode. The translation assumes the Juniper interface names match the Cisco ones (ge-1/0/0 for GigabitEthernet1/0/0, etc.).', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 point-to-point'}]]": 1,
    "['isis metric [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 level 2 metric 10', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco \"isis metric 10\" command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 level 2 metric 10\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 level 2 metric 10\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses hierarchical configuration, so we specify the IS-IS protocol context first\\n2. \"ge-1/0/0\" and \"ge-2/0/0\" are Juniper\\'s equivalent interface naming for GigabitEthernet\\n3. We explicitly set the metric at \"level 2\" since the Cisco config specified \"is-type level-2-only\"\\n4. Both interfaces need separate commands in Juniper (unlike Cisco where it\\'s configured under each interface)', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 level 2 metric 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 level 2 metric 10', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco \"isis metric 10\" command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 level 2 metric 10\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 level 2 metric 10\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses hierarchical configuration, so we specify the IS-IS protocol context first\\n2. \"ge-1/0/0\" and \"ge-2/0/0\" are Juniper\\'s equivalent interface naming for GigabitEthernet\\n3. We explicitly set the metric at \"level 2\" since the Cisco config specified \"is-type level-2-only\"\\n4. Both interfaces need separate commands in Juniper (unlike Cisco where it\\'s configured under each interface)', 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 level 2 metric 10'}]]": 1,
    "['isis network [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 point-to-point', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `isis network point-to-point` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 point-to-point\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 point-to-point\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In Juniper, we explicitly configure the point-to-point setting per interface under the IS-IS protocol configuration\\n2. The interface naming would follow Juniper's convention (ge-x/x/x instead of GigabitEthernet)\\n3. Unlike Cisco where the command is interface-level, Juniper configures this under the protocol hierarchy\\n4. Both interfaces from the original config are included since they both had the point-to-point setting\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 point-to-point'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 point-to-point', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `isis network point-to-point` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 point-to-point\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 point-to-point\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In Juniper, we explicitly configure the point-to-point setting per interface under the IS-IS protocol configuration\\n2. The interface naming would follow Juniper's convention (ge-x/x/x instead of GigabitEthernet)\\n3. Unlike Cisco where the command is interface-level, Juniper configures this under the protocol hierarchy\\n4. Both interfaces from the original config are included since they both had the point-to-point setting\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 point-to-point'}]]": 1,
    "['isis metric [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 level 2 metric 10', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco command `isis metric 10`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 level 2 metric 10\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 level 2 metric 10\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper requires specifying the IS-IS level (level 2 in this case, matching Cisco's `is-type level-2-only`)\\n2. The interface naming follows Juniper's format (ge-1/0/0 instead of GigabitEthernet1/0/0)\\n3. Since the metric was applied to both interfaces in Cisco, both translations are provided\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 level 2 metric 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 level 2 metric 10', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco command `isis metric 10`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0 level 2 metric 10\\nset protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 level 2 metric 10\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper requires specifying the IS-IS level (level 2 in this case, matching Cisco's `is-type level-2-only`)\\n2. The interface naming follows Juniper's format (ge-1/0/0 instead of GigabitEthernet1/0/0)\\n3. Since the metric was applied to both interfaces in Cisco, both translations are provided\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-2/0/0 level 2 metric 10'}]]": 1,
